From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller 9995: give the TTLM policy file a trigger

Patch 9994 generates the TID-to-Link Mapping policy into the AP MLD Config
Request. Tried on hardware for the first time today, it never sent one.

cntlr_renew_nodes_configuration() pushes the request when

	node->last_apmld_ack < cfg.last_apmld_change

and last_apmld_change only moves inside the CONFIG_DIFF_AP_MLD branch of the
config reload (config.c:3749, :3759). A plain file cannot produce a UCI diff, so
writing a policy moved nothing, `ubus call map.controller reconf` answered
"Configuration reloaded, no changes detected", and cntlr_gen_tid_to_link_policy()
was never reached. Restarting the controller does not help either: with an
unchanged config there is no diff, so last_apmld_change stays zero and the
comparison is false for every node.

The code was right and unreachable. This makes it reachable: watch the file's
mtime on the periodic tick and move that same timestamp when it changes. The
existing machinery then sends to every agent and re-sends until each one
acknowledges - no new path and no new retry logic.

mtime rather than a content hash on purpose: the producer is mlo-steerd
rewriting the file, and a rewrite always moves mtime. Hashing would cost a read
on every tick to catch a case that cannot occur.

The first sighting after a start is not treated as a change. The agents were
configured from this same file last time round, and pushing on every restart
would put a CMDU on the air for nothing.

A removed file is not a teardown. The agents keep what they were last told;
tearing a mapping down is a policy line of its own, not the absence of one.

diff -urN a/src/cntlr.c b/src/cntlr.c
--- a/src/cntlr.c	2026-08-01 19:44:52.959819702 +0200
+++ b/src/cntlr.c	2026-08-01 19:44:52.959967432 +0200
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <map_module.h>
 #include <signal.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
@@ -1801,6 +1802,57 @@
 		timer_set(&c->son_timer, 0);
 }
 
+#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
+/* Make a change to the TTLM policy file push itself.
+ *
+ * Patch 9994 puts the policy into the AP MLD Config Request, and the request is
+ * sent by cntlr_renew_nodes_configuration() below when
+ *
+ *	node->last_apmld_ack < cfg.last_apmld_change
+ *
+ * The catch, found the first time it was tried on hardware: last_apmld_change
+ * only ever moves inside the CONFIG_DIFF_AP_MLD branch of the config reload
+ * (config.c). A plain file cannot produce a UCI diff, so writing a policy moved
+ * nothing, `reconf` answered "no changes detected", and the generator was never
+ * called - correct code, unreachable.
+ *
+ * Watching the file's mtime and moving the same timestamp is all it takes: the
+ * existing machinery then sends the request to every agent and keeps re-sending
+ * until each one acknowledges. No new path, no new retry logic.
+ *
+ * Deliberately mtime and not a hash: the producer is mlo-steerd rewriting the
+ * whole file, and a rewrite always moves mtime. Comparing content would cost a
+ * read on every tick to catch a case that cannot happen.
+ */
+static void cntlr_check_ttlm_policy_change(struct controller *c)
+{
+	static time_t last_mtime;
+	struct stat st;
+
+	if (stat("/etc/mapc/ttlm-policy", &st)) {
+		/* File removed: nothing to push, and the agents keep whatever
+		 * they were last told. Tearing a mapping down is a policy line
+		 * of its own, not the absence of one. */
+		last_mtime = 0;
+		return;
+	}
+
+	if (st.st_mtime == last_mtime)
+		return;
+
+	/* First sighting after a start is not a change - the agents were
+	 * configured from this same file the last time round, and pushing on
+	 * every restart would put a CMDU on the air for nothing. */
+	if (last_mtime) {
+		dbg("%s: ttlm-policy changed, scheduling AP MLD Config Request\n",
+		    __func__);
+		timestamp_update(&c->cfg.last_apmld_change);
+	}
+
+	last_mtime = st.st_mtime;
+}
+#endif
+
 static void cntlr_renew_nodes_configuration(struct controller *c)
 {
 	trace("%s: --->\n", __func__);
@@ -1808,6 +1860,12 @@
 	struct node *node = NULL;
 	char ev_data[256] = {0};
 
+#if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
+	/* before the loop, so a policy written since the last tick is already
+	 * visible to the per-node comparison below */
+	cntlr_check_ttlm_policy_change(c);
+#endif
+
 	/* When at least one running node was configured with older config, */
 	/* send autoconfig renew */
 	list_for_each_entry(node, &c->agentlist, list) {
